'''Kulhudhuffushi Airport''' ({{airport codes|HDK|VRBK|p=n}}) is an [[airport]] located on the city of [[Kulhudhuffushi]]<ref name="WAD">{{usurped|1=[https://web.archive.org/web/20190826174401/http://worldaerodata.com/wad.cgi?airport=VRBK Airport information for VRBK]}} from [[DAFIF]] (effective October 2006)</ref> in [[Haa Dhaalu Atoll]], [[Maldives]]. The construction of the airport began on 28 October 2017 and it was officially opened on 21 September 2018, while commercial operations began on 9 August 2019.<ref>{{Cite news |date=8 August 2019 |title=Scheduled flights to Kulhudhuffushi Airport to begin on Friday |url=https://maldivestimes.com/scheduled-flights-to-kulhudhuffushi-airport-to-begin-on-friday/ |url-status=dead |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20190809144628/https://maldivestimes.com/scheduled-flights-to-kulhudhuffushi-airport-to-begin-on-friday/ |archive-date=2019-08-09 |access-date=2019-08-09 |work=Maldives Times}}</ref><ref>{{Cite web |title=Kulhudhuffushi Airport |url=https://airports.mv/airports#HDK |access-date=26 January 2024 |website=Maldives Airports Company Limited}}</ref>

==Facilities==
The airport resides at an [[elevation]] of {{convert|1|m|0}} above [[mean sea level]]. It has one [[runway]] designated 12/30 with an [[Asphalt concrete|asphalt]] surface measuring {{convert|1220|x|30|m|0}}.<ref name="WAD" />

